scriba (1.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sync with upstream 1.1.1: a documentation release. The guide's redaction and
    hot reconfiguration sections now say what a JSON line carries, what an unset
    seam does and what the read costs; the README and the comparison table name
    both features; and the pipeline diagram shows the redaction step.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:55:00 +0100

scriba (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sync with upstream 1.1.0: a redaction layer that masks the values of named
    context keys before any layout renders them (default-redacted-keys), and a
    hot reconfiguration seam (current-logger, set-current-logger!) that a
    sigaction handler can swap without breaking ahead-of-time level filtering.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:25:00 +0100

